WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.770
Speaker 1: David, is it likely that if Trump
runs in 2004, he will be unopposed in the

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.220
Republican primary?

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:11.910
No, Trump, if he runs in twenty four, Trump
will almost certainly be opposed.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.879
The question is whether it will be a serious
challenger.

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:20.039
We could if we were to imagine what is the
most serious challenge that Donald Trump could

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:21.640
face.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.680
One school of thought would be somebody like
Mitt Romney runs an anti Trump Republican

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.000
with some name recognition.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.210
I don't know that Romney gets more than 10
or maybe 15 percent in a Republican primary.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:38.170
I think the way things are right now, Trump
owns the Republican Party.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.600
Trump crushes basically whoever tries to run
against him.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:48.510
The one name that seems to have more power
against Trump would be Ron DeSantis, who is

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:54.280
essentially a more competent Trump, which
is extraordinarily dangerous even to seems

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.579
to have only low 20s.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:59.960
I think in a couple of recent straw polls,
it was something like twenty one twenty two

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.179
percent support or something like that.

00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:06.860
So at this point in time, this nomination
is Trump's for the taking.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.600
If he wants it, if he wants it, I don't think
anybody else is going to be able to mount

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.600
a successful challenge.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.880
You know, people talk about what about Lisa
Murkowski or something?

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.390
No, I just don't see it.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:17.960
I just don't see the name recognition.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:23.290
I just don't see the interest level, so to
speak, in supporting her over Trump when Trump

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:29.229
is sort of the de facto and as of as of today,
still widely supported by the Republican Party.

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:33.810
I think that Trump's perspective on this let
me go back.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.369
When I was on Michael Cohen's podcast a couple
of weeks ago, Michael Cohen said he doesn't

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:41.820
think ultimately that Donald Trump runs.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.799
And he had a number of different reasons that
he gave.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:45.710
We uploaded that to our YouTube channel.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.590
And you can check that out if you want to
hear more about that.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:55.509
But one of the arguments about why Trump ultimately
won't run is Trump is able to raise money

00:01:55.509 --> 00:02:02.860
and benefit from kind of alluding to running
and doing events and asking people to donate

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:08.840
to the Save America PAC or whatever, but not
actually saying I'm running and maybe never

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:09.870
actually running.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:15.471
The idea being raised as much money as he
can get as much attention as possible, paralyze

00:02:15.471 --> 00:02:20.480
the party so the party can't say, OK, he's
not running, but they also can't say he is

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.480
running.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.620
As for as long as Trump is doing speeches
and talking about I think you'll like what

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:30.020
we decide, but not announcing a candidacy,
he paralyzes the Republican Party.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.500
He keeps people under his thumb.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.720
And that's exactly what Donald Trump wants
to do.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.610
And he can just keep grifting his supporters.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:40.460
New report he raised, who knows, tens of millions
of dollars over the last six months, claiming

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.500
it's all to fight the election results.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.310
He has spent no money on fighting the election
results because the election was nine months

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.730
ago and nothing is going to change.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.060
But that's what Trump wants to do.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.230
He wants to keep raising money.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:57.050
So I also see that even if Trump is not ultimately
going to run, it's very much to his advantage

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.950
to pretend that he is.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:04.790
My instinct is if he's healthy and twenty
twenty two goes OK for the Trump wing of the

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.130
party Trump runs, that's my opinion.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:10.290
Only Michael Cohen said I think he he doesn't
run.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.740
In the end, an ego is a factor.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.680
And a few other things we will just have to
wait and see.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:23.680
But the best case scenario for Trump would
be that this, if he is ultimately going to

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.290
run, that keeping this situation in limbo
prevents the Republican Party from really

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:34.260
getting behind anybody else in particular,
it prevents other people from really building

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.040
support because Trump still has the majority
of the electorate supporting him.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.250
And then he says, I'm running if that's indeed
what he's going to do and he doesn't even

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.480
give oxygen to a possible serious primary
challenge.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:53.000
The other thing would be, what if Trump runs
third party?

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.130
I don't even really want to get into that
right now because I see it as very, very unlikely.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.500
But if you're if the scenario you think is
the most likely as Trump runs third party,

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:22.850
I would love to hear 

00:04:22.850 --> 00:05:35.780
from you.

